# Architecture Documentation

## System Overview

Retrofit ADAS follows **MVVM + Clean Architecture** pattern, separating concerns into three distinct layers.

## Layer Diagram

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph Presentation["Presentation Layer"]
        UI[Jetpack Compose Screens]
        VM[ViewModels]     
        NAV[Navigation]
    end

    subgraph Domain["Domain Layer"]
        UC[Use Cases]
        MOD[Domain Models]
        REPO_I[Repository Interfaces]
    end

    subgraph Data["Data Layer"]
        REPO_IMPL[Repository Implementations]
        OBD[OBD-II Connection Manager]
        SENSOR[Sensor Reader]
        FUSION[Sensor Fusion Engine]
        DB[Room Database]
    end

    subgraph External["External"]
        BT[Bluetooth / ELM327]
        PHONE[Phone Sensors]
        GPS[GPS / Location]
    end

    UI --> VM
    VM --> UC
    UC --> REPO_I
    REPO_I -.-> REPO_IMPL
    REPO_IMPL --> OBD
    REPO_IMPL --> DB
    OBD --> BT
    SENSOR --> PHONE
    FUSION --> OBD
    FUSION --> SENSOR
    FUSION --> GPS
```

## Data Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant V as Vehicle (OBD-II)
    participant BT as Bluetooth
    participant OBD as ObdConnectionManager
    participant SF as SensorFusionEngine
    participant UC as Use Cases
    participant VM as DashboardViewModel
    participant UI as DashboardScreen

    V->>BT: Raw OBD Data
    BT->>OBD: ELM327 Response
    OBD->>OBD: Parse PIDs (Speed, RPM, Temp)
    OBD->>SF: VehicleData Flow
    SF->>SF: Combine with Accelerometer
    SF->>UC: FusedData Flow
    UC->>UC: Check Speed Limit
    UC->>UC: Detect Harsh Braking
    UC->>VM: Alert / VehicleData
    VM->>UI: UiState Update
    UI->>UI: Recompose (Speed Gauge, Alerts)
```

